## Context

The memory design reached v3 after three external reviews and a working session
with the author. `docs/2026-09-10-dragon-memory-design.md` is the settled architecture; this ticket tracks
turning it into code. It stays open until every child is merged and the
integration review in `/roar` step 8 has run.

The architecture in one paragraph: the store is the bodies, one file per memory
under git; `MEMORY.md` is generated as the top N by score and never
hand-edited; nothing is ever deleted, and the only removal from a project
directory is promotion into the harness tier; a memory declares what it is true
*while*, and expiry only unranks, so it is reversible.

## Children

- `0908` — promotion marks the project copy dead in the form the walker reads
- `0910` — generate the memory index as the top N of its directory
- `0911` — one type field, one frontmatter shape, `valid_while` and `supersedes`
- `0912` — consolidation pass: pool, dedupe, promote, tombstone

Only `0912` has a real prerequisite (`0908`). The other three are independent.

## Deliberately not children

A decay pass, a corpus cap, an orphan collector, and a full-catalogue file. §5
of the design removes the need for all four; they are listed here so a later
reader does not re-derive them as gaps.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] All four children merged
- [ ] Child diffs re-read together, not only individually
- [ ] `make check` passes on the union
- [ ] The design's §6 matches what shipped, or the design is amended to match
